#!/bin/sh
# The owner's page: `pi web serve` from admin.env, as `pia` runs `pi`, with no terminal and no
# lifetime of its own. The entrypoint starts this as pi with piweb its primary group, in the
# background, with an empty environment, as it starts http-serve. So the page's socket,
# <PI_KEY_FILE>.web, is made in the group piweb, whose one other member is pitail, the user
# `tailscale serve` runs as; the server makes it 0660 and its control socket,
# <PI_KEY_FILE>.web-control, 0600. Core dumps are off: the server holds the key file. Its log lines
# (stderr) go to /data/pi/web.log; its stdout goes nowhere, so a login code is never kept on the
# volume.
#
# `--agent-journal`: the page appends to the erasure journal as pi (a lift of a release among its writes), so
# after each write that changed it the server hands the journal's mark to the agent API's two copies as the
# timer does, through pi's sudo rules for pimcp and pihttp to lib/agent-file journal. A failure is one
# agent_journal_failed line in web.log.
#
# Run by the box's one supervisor (lib/supervise), with its start and end
# lines, its backoff (a server that ends within a minute of its start, before the schema or before
# `pia erase replay`, waits longer each time) and its rotation by size during the run. One that ends
# with 3, stopped by `pia web stop`, is not started again until the box restarts.
ulimit -c 0
exec /usr/local/lib/pi/supervise web /data/pi/web.log --state /run/pistate/web.restarts --stdout null --stop 3 -- /usr/local/lib/pi/run admin web serve --agent-journal
